{%- comment -%}
  The display label for one facet value - or nothing at all, meaning hide this value.

  Accepts: filter (required), value (required)

  Why this exists. The question "is this the Color filter, and is this value a real colour?"
  was asked in six places in snippets/facets.liquid, with TWO different conditions:

    the two checkbox lists    filter.label | downcase == 'color'
    the four active pills     filter.label == 'Color' or filter.label == 'color'

  Those are not equivalent. A filter labelled COLOUR or Colour satisfies the first and not
  the second, so the checkbox list would read "Blue" while the pill above it read
  "color-blue". The ~55-name whitelist itself was pasted out in full twice. Six copies, two
  meanings, and nothing fails when one is edited.

  Behaviour:
    not the Color filter  -> the value's own label, unchanged
    a whitelisted colour  -> the colour name, prefix stripped and capitalised
    anything else         -> nothing, so the caller hides the value

  The whitelist is still a whitelist, because the Color facet is fed from tags and the tag
  namespace carries non-colours. It now fails in one place instead of two. R28 records that
  all 13 live color-* tags pass it as of 2026-09-16; a fourteenth colour added in admin will
  vanish from the facet until it is added here, which is the known cost of this approach.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign cf_filter_lower = filter.label | downcase

  if cf_filter_lower == 'color' or cf_filter_lower == 'colour'
    assign cf_whitelist = 'pink,red,orange,yellow,green,blue,purple,brown,beige,white,gray,grey,black,multi,navy,teal,coral,ivory,cream,gold,silver,rose,lavender,mint,burgundy,maroon,tan,khaki,olive,turquoise,magenta,peach,charcoal,indigo,aqua,mauve,plum,rust,salmon,taupe,wine,amber,bronze,champagne,copper,crimson,emerald,fuchsia,jade,lilac,mustard,sage,sapphire,scarlet,slate,violet' | split: ','
    assign cf_stripped = value.label | downcase | remove_first: 'color-'
    for cf_name in cf_whitelist
      if cf_stripped == cf_name
        echo cf_stripped | capitalize
        break
      endif
    endfor
  else
    echo value.label
  endif
-%}
